"Let the latest open/change event own the single overlay entry, falling back to the next recent alias when it closes. Compute facts for that chosen content and send findings only to aliases with matching bytes. Older conflicting documents cannot request results; a visible divergence warning explains the choice. Versioned edits may target the winner, and the cache incorporates every alias event.",
"Use event recency to select one canonical buffer, promoting the most recent survivor after close. The selected text supplies analysis and only agreeing URIs receive its diagnostics; conflicting earlier aliases get query refusals. Show the conflict while allowing atomic versioned edits on the selected document, with all alias events participating in identity checks."
